{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "frozen independent structural development variants; CPU contracts are not model quality evidence",
  "criteria": {
    "relation_scope_v1": "The last assistant's text has a source-grounding risk if any factual assertion lacks support from, or contradicts, the provided documents when its complete relation is considered. Preserve the object, value, unit, comparator, per-item versus aggregate scope, inclusion or exclusion, negation, and explicit conditions, exceptions, versions and roles together. A value supported for a different object or condition does not support the assertion. Separate table rows do not by themselves establish containment, addition, or a performance guarantee. Apply explicit source conditions and valid deductions from supplied relations, including unit conversions; do not require a supported deduction to be stated verbatim. Conversation history may resolve references, but prior assistant assertions are not source evidence. Assess a statement that the sources do not answer the current question against all provided documents: a justified evidence-limited abstention is not a risk, whereas denying an answer explicitly available in the sources is a risk. Judge the current answer, not the truth of every previous conversation turn.",
    "citation_binding_v1": "The last assistant's text has a citation-binding risk if a cited evidence identifier has no matching provided document, or if the document or documents explicitly cited for a factual assertion do not support that assertion with its object, value, unit, scope and conditions. Match bracketed evidence identifiers to document doc_id values. A comma-separated group cites its listed documents jointly; combine them only when their contents support the asserted relation. Support available only in an uncited document does not repair the citation. Prior assistant assertions are not source evidence. Evaluate the actual citations in the current answer, not citations in conversation history. Do not infer that uncited assertions are correct or incorrect, and do not treat citation presence alone as support."
  },
  "expected_semantics": "true=criterion risk, false=no criterion risk, null=not covered; expectations never enter model payload",
